  "passage": "A student found an online article saying a local festival began in 1920. Another source said 1932.\nInstead of choosing the first result, she visited the library archive. Old newspaper records showed that a small version began in 1920, but the official yearly festival started in 1932.\nBoth dates were partly right.\nHer report explained the difference.\nThe project taught her that research is not always about finding one source and copying it. Sometimes facts have layers.\nGood research asks why sources disagree. The answer may reveal a richer story than either source alone.",
